From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:25:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Give the admin panel a Notifications inbox: unread badge,
 mark-read, and feeds
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The panel's Notifications tab shows two kinds of row: the API's own event rows
(targetType ADMINS — new order, salon registration, renewal, delivery-partner
action, booking request, written by backend-9) and the pushes an admin sent from
the screen. This adds the endpoints that make it a real inbox:

* `POST /api/adminNotification/get-admin-notification-count` — unread event
  rows, for the sidebar badge. Always answers SUCCESS with a number (0 on a
  fresh install or a read failure), because a badge is not worth an error.
* `POST /api/adminNotification/mark-admin-notifications-read` — marks the event
  rows read, so opening the tab clears the badge. It never touches an admin's
  own sent rows: those were never unread messages to them.
* `get-admin-notification-list` accepts `feed` (`events` / `sent` / empty for
  both) and the conditions are now ANDed — the old shape replaced the whole
  `where[Op.or]` with the search term, so typing anything into the box widened
  the list beyond the admin's own rows.

`npm run notification:test-inbox` is a database-free self-check of all of it.

Apply after backend-9.
